  title: Arab Merchants 1820s
  info: "Arab traders arrived in Singapore and quickly became influential in commerce
    and religion. They established Kampong Glam as a center for Islamic culture,
    building landmarks like Sultan Mosque. Their contributions to trade, education,
    and philanthropy enriched Singapore\u2019s cultural landscape and fostered lasting
    ties with the Muslim community.  "
